 ## Overview
-The Vessel Voxelizer converts vascular structures, defined as line segments with associated radii, into a fuzzy 3D voxel volume where each voxel's value represents the fraction of its volume occupied by the vessels [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from standard binary voxelization by using supersampling to estimate the continuous volume intersection, making it suitable for rendering translucent or semi-transparent vascular networks [S1, unofficial].
+The Vessel Voxelizer converts vascular structures, defined as line segments with associated radii, into a fuzzy 3D voxel volume where each voxel's value represents the fraction of its volume occupied by the vessels [S1, unofficial]. It uses supersampling to estimate the continuous volume intersection, calculating the ratio of sample points within the vessel radius to the total number of points per voxel [S1, unofficial].
 
